{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PKqCjRxqwtLAVZAKZuSK1D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd090-chgrp\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/chgrp: Change Group Ownership\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD chgrp that differs from GNU chgrp in recursive traversal flags\n6\t  and symlink handling options. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n7\t  reference binary (gchgrp, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag\n8\t  combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Change the group ownership of files.\n12\t  - G2: Support recursive ownership changes with -R and symlink traversal control.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchgrp via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Group ownership change\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must accept a GROUP argument (name or numeric GID) and one or more FILE arguments, changing each file's group to GROUP.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's group to match RFILE's group.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the group change to each.\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the group is invalid, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Recursive and symlink handling\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-R or --recursive must change group ownership recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must change the symlink itself rather than the target. Without -h, must change the target.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: \"-H must follow symlinks given on the command line but not in recursive traversal. -L must follow all symlinks. -P must never follow symlinks (default with -R).\"\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Output control and exit codes\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed. -c or --changes must print only when changes are made. -f or --silent must suppress most errors.\"\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/chgrp does not implement --preserve-root.\n50\t\n51\tacceptance_criteria:\n52\t  - id: AC1\n53\t    criterion: \"chgrp staff file changes group to staff, matching gchgrp.\"\n54\t    traces:\n55\t      - R1.1\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t  - id: AC2\n58\t    criterion: \"chgrp -R staff dir recursively changes group, matching gchgrp -R.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R2.1\n61\t  - id: AC3\n62\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gchgrp passes for all required test cases.\"\n63\t    traces:\n64\t      - R1.1\n65\t      - R1.2\n66\t      - R2.1\n67\t  - id: AC4\n68\t    criterion: \"cmd/chgrp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n69\t    traces:\n70\t      - R1.1\n71\t      - R1.2\n72\t      - R1.3\n73\t      - R1.4\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R2.3\n77\t      - R3.1\n78\t      - R3.2\n79\t      - R3.3\n80\t\n81\tpackage_contract:\n82\t  imports:\n83\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3781725-c8fe-478c-afba-9a79c345d7fe","uuid":"20aff299-4828-4dd8-8d7b-dea84028ba32","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:12:31.149Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd090-chgrp.yaml","content":"id: srd090-chgrp\ntitle: \"cmd/chgrp: Change Group Ownership\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD chgrp that differs from GNU chgrp in recursive traversal flags\n  and symlink handling options. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU\n  reference binary (gchgrp, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag\n  combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Change the group ownership of files.\n  - G2: Support recursive ownership changes with -R and symlink traversal control.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchgrp via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Group ownership change\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must accept a GROUP argument (name or numeric GID) and one or more FILE arguments, changing each file's group to GROUP.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's group to match RFILE's group.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must process multiple FILE arguments, applying the group change to each.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the group is invalid, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Recursive and symlink handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-R or --recursive must change group ownership recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must change the symlink itself rather than the target. Without -h, must change the target.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-H must follow symlinks given on the command line but not in recursive traversal. -L must follow all symlinks. -P must never follow symlinks (default with -R).\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Output control and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed. -c or --changes must print only when changes are made. -f or --silent must suppress most errors.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/chgrp does not implement --preserve-root.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"chgrp staff file changes group to staff, matching gchgrp.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"chgrp -R staff dir recursively changes group, matching gchgrp -R.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gchgrp passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/chgrp compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
