{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ue8cbbAapwv8A1sCLeSouv","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive view. Let me create a summary of all the diagnostic output patterns I found:\n\n## Summary of Verbose/Diagnostic Output Patterns\n\nBased on my search through the go-unix-utils repository, here are the key patterns found:\n\n### 1. **chmod** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/chmod/main.go`)\n\n**Diagnostic Function:**\n```go\nfunc printDiagnostic(opts options, path string, oldMode, newMode os.FileMode) {\n\tif opts.verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\",\n\t\t\tpath, uint32(oldMode), symbolicString(oldMode), uint32(newMode), symbolicString(newMode))\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif opts.changes && oldMode != newMode {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\",\n\t\t\tpath, uint32(oldMode), symbolicString(oldMode), uint32(newMode), symbolicString(newMode))\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- Function named `printDiagnostic` at lines 142-152\n- Message format: `\"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\"`\n- Shows octal AND symbolic representation (e.g., `0755 (rwxr-xr-x)`)\n- Handles both `-v/--verbose` (reports every file) and `-c/--changes` (reports only when changed)\n- Uses `symbolicString()` helper to convert mode bits to rwxst notation\n\n**Mode to Symbolic Conversion:**\n```go\nfunc symbolicString(mode os.FileMode) string {\n\tvar buf [9]byte\n\tconst rwx = \"rwx\"\n\tfor i := range 9 {\n\t\tif mode&(1<<uint(8-i)) != 0 {\n\t\t\tbuf[i] = rwx[i%3]\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tbuf[i] = '-'\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tapplySpecialBits(&buf, mode)  // Applies s/t for setuid/setgid/sticky\n\treturn string(buf[:])\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **chgrp** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/chgrp/main.go`)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Line 100-115: `lookupGroup()` function uses `os/user` package:\n```go\nfunc lookupGroup(group string) int {\n\tif gid, err := strconv.Atoi(group); err == nil {\n\t\treturn gid\n\t}\n\tg, err := user.LookupGroup(group)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", group)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(g.Gid)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", group)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn gid\n}\n```\n\n- **Note:** chgrp does NOT have verbose diagnostic output implemented yet (lines 127-144 show applyChown and changeGroup but no print statements)\n\n**Reference Resolution:**\n```go\nfunc resolveReference(rfile string) int {\n\tfi, err := sys.Stat(rfile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: failed to get attributes of '%s': %s\\n\",\n\t\t\trfile, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn int(fi.Gid)  // Extracts GID from file stats\n}\n```\n\n- Uses `pkg/sys.Stat()` which provides extended metadata including `Gid` field (line 125)\n\n### 3. **rm** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/rm/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nif opts.verbose {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"removed '%s'\\n\", path)      // line 189 (files)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"removed directory '%s'\\n\", path)  // line 223 (dirs)\n}\n```\n\n- Simple output format without state comparison\n- Prints on successful removal only\n\n### 4. **mkdir** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/mkdir/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nif verbose {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mkdir: created directory '%s'\\n\", dir)  // lines 97, 142\n}\n```\n\n- Simple informational message on directory creation\n\n### 5. **cp** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/cp/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(src, dest string) {\n\tif verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"'%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)  // line 404\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Called at lines 296, 331, 356 (after directory, symlink, and file copies)\n- No state information, just source -> destination\n\n### 6. **mv** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/mv/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(src, dest string, renamed bool) {\n\tif renamed {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"renamed '%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"'%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Line 266-272: Distinguishes between rename (same filesystem) and copy+delete operations\n- Called at lines 171, 199\n\n### 7. **ln** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/ln/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(backupPath, linkName, arrow, target string) {\n\tif backupPath != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"'%s' ~ '%s' %s '%s'\\n\", backupPath, linkName, arrow, target)\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"'%s' %s '%s'\\n\", linkName, arrow, target)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Lines 155-161: Uses `->` for symlinks, `=>` for hard links (line 150)\n- Includes backup file info if one was created\n\n### Key Patterns Summary:\n\n1. **Diagnostic function naming:** `printDiagnostic`, `printVerbose`\n2. **Before/after comparison:** Only chmod shows old/new state\n3. **Format strings:** Usually `\"<verb> '%s'\\n\"` or `\"'%s' <arrow> '%s'\\n\"`\n4. **User/group lookup:** Use Go's standard `os/user` package for name lookup by GID/UID\n5. **Reference resolution:** Use `pkg/sys.Stat()` to get extended metadata including Uid/Gid\n6. **Verbose flag patterns:** Check `opts.verbose` or `opts.changes` before printing\n7. **No diagnostic output in chgrp yet** - only error reporting, no success messages"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3781725-c8fe-478c-afba-9a79c345d7fe","uuid":"41504621-587a-4343-8e5f-b5d35838e255","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:14:33.198Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In this Go coreutils reimplementation repo, find examples of how other cmd/ utilities (especially cmd/chown if it exists) implement verbose/changes diagnostic output. Look for patterns like:\n1. \"changed group of\" or \"changed owner of\" or \"retained as\" strings\n2. Functions named printDiagnostic, reportChange, or similar\n3. How they look up group/user names from GIDs/UIDs\n\nSearch in cmd/chown/, cmd/chmod/ and any other utilities that have verbose output. Show the relevant code snippets.","agentId":"a48ca9f472c497a87","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive view. Let me create a summary of all the diagnostic output patterns I found:\n\n## Summary of Verbose/Diagnostic Output Patterns\n\nBased on my search through the go-unix-utils repository, here are the key patterns found:\n\n### 1. **chmod** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/chmod/main.go`)\n\n**Diagnostic Function:**\n```go\nfunc printDiagnostic(opts options, path string, oldMode, newMode os.FileMode) {\n\tif opts.verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\",\n\t\t\tpath, uint32(oldMode), symbolicString(oldMode), uint32(newMode), symbolicString(newMode))\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\tif opts.changes && oldMode != newMode {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\",\n\t\t\tpath, uint32(oldMode), symbolicString(oldMode), uint32(newMode), symbolicString(newMode))\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- Function named `printDiagnostic` at lines 142-152\n- Message format: `\"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\"`\n- Shows octal AND symbolic representation (e.g., `0755 (rwxr-xr-x)`)\n- Handles both `-v/--verbose` (reports every file) and `-c/--changes` (reports only when changed)\n- Uses `symbolicString()` helper to convert mode bits to rwxst notation\n\n**Mode to Symbolic Conversion:**\n```go\nfunc symbolicString(mode os.FileMode) string {\n\tvar buf [9]byte\n\tconst rwx = \"rwx\"\n\tfor i := range 9 {\n\t\tif mode&(1<<uint(8-i)) != 0 {\n\t\t\tbuf[i] = rwx[i%3]\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tbuf[i] = '-'\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tapplySpecialBits(&buf, mode)  // Applies s/t for setuid/setgid/sticky\n\treturn string(buf[:])\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **chgrp** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/chgrp/main.go`)\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Line 100-115: `lookupGroup()` function uses `os/user` package:\n```go\nfunc lookupGroup(group string) int {\n\tif gid, err := strconv.Atoi(group); err == nil {\n\t\treturn gid\n\t}\n\tg, err := user.LookupGroup(group)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", group)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(g.Gid)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", group)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn gid\n}\n```\n\n- **Note:** chgrp does NOT have verbose diagnostic output implemented yet (lines 127-144 show applyChown and changeGroup but no print statements)\n\n**Reference Resolution:**\n```go\nfunc resolveReference(rfile string) int {\n\tfi, err := sys.Stat(rfile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chgrp: failed to get attributes of '%s': %s\\n\",\n\t\t\trfile, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn int(fi.Gid)  // Extracts GID from file stats\n}\n```\n\n- Uses `pkg/sys.Stat()` which provides extended metadata including `Gid` field (line 125)\n\n### 3. **rm** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/rm/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nif opts.verbose {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"removed '%s'\\n\", path)      // line 189 (files)\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"removed directory '%s'\\n\", path)  // line 223 (dirs)\n}\n```\n\n- Simple output format without state comparison\n- Prints on successful removal only\n\n### 4. **mkdir** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/mkdir/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nif verbose {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"mkdir: created directory '%s'\\n\", dir)  // lines 97, 142\n}\n```\n\n- Simple informational message on directory creation\n\n### 5. **cp** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/cp/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(src, dest string) {\n\tif verbose {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"'%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)  // line 404\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Called at lines 296, 331, 356 (after directory, symlink, and file copies)\n- No state information, just source -> destination\n\n### 6. **mv** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/mv/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(src, dest string, renamed bool) {\n\tif renamed {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"renamed '%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Printf(\"'%s' -> '%s'\\n\", src, dest)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Line 266-272: Distinguishes between rename (same filesystem) and copy+delete operations\n- Called at lines 171, 199\n\n### 7. **ln** (`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/cmd/ln/main.go`)\n\n**Verbose Output Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc printVerbose(backupPath, linkName, arrow, target string) {\n\tif backupPath != \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"'%s' ~ '%s' %s '%s'\\n\", backupPath, linkName, arrow, target)\n\t} else {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"'%s' %s '%s'\\n\", linkName, arrow, target)\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n- Lines 155-161: Uses `->` for symlinks, `=>` for hard links (line 150)\n- Includes backup file info if one was created\n\n### Key Patterns Summary:\n\n1. **Diagnostic function naming:** `printDiagnostic`, `printVerbose`\n2. **Before/after comparison:** Only chmod shows old/new state\n3. **Format strings:** Usually `\"<verb> '%s'\\n\"` or `\"'%s' <arrow> '%s'\\n\"`\n4. **User/group lookup:** Use Go's standard `os/user` package for name lookup by GID/UID\n5. **Reference resolution:** Use `pkg/sys.Stat()` to get extended metadata including Uid/Gid\n6. **Verbose flag patterns:** Check `opts.verbose` or `opts.changes` before printing\n7. **No diagnostic output in chgrp yet** - only error reporting, no success messages"}],"totalDurationMs":37645,"totalTokens":52707,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":49417,"output_tokens":2072,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1214},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2072,"cache_read_input_tokens":49417,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1214,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":8,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
