{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018yjHTEr2WTXTXqdvvEQF4e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// Package testutils provides the differential testing harness for go-unix-utils.\n5\t// It executes a Go binary and a GNU reference binary with identical inputs and\n6\t// compares stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n7\t// Implements srd001-testutils.\n8\tpackage testutils\n9\t\n10\timport (\n11\t\t\"bytes\"\n12\t\t\"context\"\n13\t\t\"errors\"\n14\t\t\"fmt\"\n15\t\t\"os\"\n16\t\t\"os/exec\"\n17\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n18\t\t\"regexp\"\n19\t\t\"strings\"\n20\t\t\"testing\"\n21\t\t\"time\"\n22\t)\n23\t\n24\tconst defaultTimeout = 10 * time.Second\n25\t\n26\t// NormalizeFunc transforms raw output bytes before comparison.\n27\t// R1.4: named type alias for normalization functions.\n28\ttype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n29\t\n30\t// DiffTest defines a single differential test case.\n31\t//\n32\t// R1.1: Name identifies the subtest (used with t.Run). Args holds command-line\n33\t// arguments passed to both binaries.\n34\t//\n35\t// R1.2: Stdin nil means both binaries receive EOF immediately. An empty non-nil\n36\t// slice ([]byte{}) also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin that is\n37\t// immediately closed. ExitCode defaults to 0 when left as the zero value.\n38\t//\n39\t// R1.3: Env nil means both binaries inherit the test process environment with\n40\t// LC_ALL=C applied as a default override. When non-nil, KEY=VALUE pairs are\n41\t// merged into the inherited environment: matching keys are overridden, new keys\n42\t// are added.\n43\t//\n44\t// R1.4: Normalize holds a slice of NormalizeFunc applied in order to stdout and\n45\t// stderr of both binaries before comparison. Nil or empty means no normalization.\n46\ttype DiffTest struct {\n47\t\tName          string\n48\t\tArgs          []string\n49\t\tStdin         []byte\n50\t\tEnv           []string\n51\t\tWorkDir       string\n52\t\tExitCode      int\n53\t\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n54\t\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\tvar tsPatterns = []*regexp.Regexp{\n58\t\tregexp.MustCompile(`[A-Z][a-z]{2}\\s+\\d{1,2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n59\t\tregexp.MustCompile(`\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n60\t\tregexp.MustCompile(`\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n61\t}\n62\t\n63\t// TimestampNormalizer replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed\n64\t// placeholder string.\n65\t// R4.2: built-in normalizer for cmd/ts tests.\n66\tvar TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc = func(b []byte) []byte {\n67\t\tresult := b\n68\t\tfor _, pat := range tsPatterns {\n69\t\t\tresult = pat.ReplaceAll(result, []byte(\"<TIMESTAMP>\"))\n70\t\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3781725-c8fe-478c-afba-9a79c345d7fe","uuid":"ecef88b6-9c1c-4f08-9bfc-2be478e8dae5","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:23:33.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5554/pkg/testutils/difftest.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Package testutils provides the differential testing harness for go-unix-utils.\n// It executes a Go binary and a GNU reference binary with identical inputs and\n// compares stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n// Implements srd001-testutils.\npackage testutils\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\nconst defaultTimeout = 10 * time.Second\n\n// NormalizeFunc transforms raw output bytes before comparison.\n// R1.4: named type alias for normalization functions.\ntype NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n\n// DiffTest defines a single differential test case.\n//\n// R1.1: Name identifies the subtest (used with t.Run). Args holds command-line\n// arguments passed to both binaries.\n//\n// R1.2: Stdin nil means both binaries receive EOF immediately. An empty non-nil\n// slice ([]byte{}) also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin that is\n// immediately closed. ExitCode defaults to 0 when left as the zero value.\n//\n// R1.3: Env nil means both binaries inherit the test process environment with\n// LC_ALL=C applied as a default override. When non-nil, KEY=VALUE pairs are\n// merged into the inherited environment: matching keys are overridden, new keys\n// are added.\n//\n// R1.4: Normalize holds a slice of NormalizeFunc applied in order to stdout and\n// stderr of both binaries before comparison. Nil or empty means no normalization.\ntype DiffTest struct {\n\tName          string\n\tArgs          []string\n\tStdin         []byte\n\tEnv           []string\n\tWorkDir       string\n\tExitCode      int\n\tNormalize     []NormalizeFunc\n\tExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n}\n\nvar tsPatterns = []*regexp.Regexp{\n\tregexp.MustCompile(`[A-Z][a-z]{2}\\s+\\d{1,2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n\tregexp.MustCompile(`\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n\tregexp.MustCompile(`\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}`),\n}\n\n// TimestampNormalizer replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed\n// placeholder string.\n// R4.2: built-in normalizer for cmd/ts tests.\nvar TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc = func(b []byte) []byte {\n\tresult := b\n\tfor _, pat := range tsPatterns {\n\t\tresult = pat.ReplaceAll(result, []byte(\"<TIMESTAMP>\"))\n\t}","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":241}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011pHZzKXqtMSkAu5pK8ZP61","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no `Setup` or `Reset` callback. The DiffTest runs both binaries on the same workdir sequentially. For state-changing commands like chgrp, the first binary changes state, and the second sees different state.\n\nThe existing non-verbose tests work because:\n1. Both binaries produce no stdout/stderr on success\n2. The group change by the first binary doesn't affect the second binary's ability to also change to the same group (it's a no-op but succeeds)\n\nFor verbose tests, I need to structure the test differently. Options:\n1. Use separate work directories - but RunDiffTests uses the same workDir for both\n\n\n2. Add a `Setup` func to the DiffTest - but it doesn't exist\n3. Don't use RunDiffTests for verbose tests - run each binary separately and compare manually\n4. Make the test work by having both binaries see the same initial state - not possible with one workDir\n\nActually, I can restructure this. For \"retained\" tests, I'll set the group to the target group first so both binaries see \"retained\". For \"changed\" tests, the first binary modifies the state before the second runs, so I can't use RunDiffTests for those.\n\nLet me write separate test functions that manually run each binary, reset the state between runs, and compare the outputs directly. Looking at the existing `basic_group_change` test, it sets the file to groupA first, then runs chgrp to groupB - but this approach breaks when both binaries need to see the same initial state. to B (no output, exit 0)\n2. gchgrp: chgrp groupB file → already B, no-op (no output, exit 0)\n\nBoth produce same stdout/stderr/exit. But with -v:\n1. Go binary: chgrp -v groupB file → \"changed group of 'file' from groupA to groupB\"\n2. gchgrp: chgrp -v groupB file → \"group of 'file' retained as groupB\"\n\nDifferent stdout! Test fails.\n\nSo for